+The current `verify_single` implementation is silently failing its `httpx` requests and instantly triggering the Supabase fallback, which returns generic mockup data. I want to completely DISABLE the mockup/fallback data. 
+
+Execute these EXACT changes:
+1. In `routers/verify.py`, update the `TrustScoreResult` Pydantic model to include a new field: `projectUrl: Optional[str] = None`.
+2. In `verify_service.py`, completely REMOVE the Supabase database imports and fallback logic. Do not generate random numbers if a fetch fails.
+3. Inside `verify_single`, parse the `credit_id` and build the real-world URL:
+   - If "VCS-" is in the ID, extract the number. `project_url = f"https://registry.verra.org/app/projectDetail/VCS/{number}"`
+   - If "GOLD-" or "GS" is in the ID (like GOLD-GS13-194), extract the number. `project_url = f"https://registry.goldstandard.org/projects?q={number}"`
+   - If "ACR-" is in the ID, `project_url = "https://acr2.apx.com/myModule/rpt/myrpt.asp?r=111"`
+4. Use `httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0)` to make a GET request to that `project_url`.
+5. If the request succeeds (status 200), parse what you can, but absolutely DO NOT generate fake scores. Set `dataMode="live"` and include the `projectUrl` in the returned dictionary.
+6. If the request is blocked by Cloudflare (403) or times out, DO NOT fall back to fake data. Return a valid `TrustScoreResult` but set `trustScore=0`, `verdict="UNVERIFIED"`, `dataMode="fetch_failed"`, and ensure the `projectUrl` is still included so the frontend can display the link to the user.
+
+Do not ask questions. Disable the mock fallback, implement the real URLs, and ensure the frontend receives the `projectUrl`.

